L001354	\sec{Results}
L001355	The scattering angle $\theta_{\text{cons}}$ follows from the impulse using $|\Delta p^\mu_{i,\rm cons}|=2p_\infty\sin(\theta_{\text{cons}}/2)$.
L001356	Here $p_\infty=m_1 m_2 \sqrt{\gamma^2-1}/E$, the total (conserved) energy is $E=M\sqrt{1+2\nu(\gamma-1)}$ and the total mass is $M=m_1+m_2$, with $\nu=m_1m_2/M^2$ the symmetric mass ratio.
L001357	The scattering angle is given in PM expansion as
L001358	\begin{align}
L001359	  \label{thetadef}
L001360	    \theta_{\text{cons}}=\frac{E}{M} \sum_{m\geq1}\sum_{s=0}^{\lfloor\frac{m-1}{2}\rfloor}
L001361	    \bigg(
L001362	      \frac{GM}{|b|}
L001363	      \bigg)^m
L001364	      \nu^s
L001365	    \theta^{(m,s)}_{\text{cons}}(\gamma)\,,
L001366	  \end{align}
